WEBVTT

1
00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:19.141
"Whoa!" Jacey shouted. "Brooklyn, watch out!"

2
00:00:19.142 --> 00:00:24.573
Brooklyn tried to move out of the way before Dirk slammed into her.

3
00:00:24.574 --> 00:00:29.173
But he was moving so fast, there was almost nothing she could do.

4
00:00:29.174 --> 00:00:33.821
Dirk crashed into Brooklyn, who crashed into Coach Teagan.

5
00:00:33.822 --> 00:00:41.651
The coach fell down hard on the gym floor while something else flew up into the air.

6
00:00:41.652 --> 00:00:44.566
"My phone!" the coach cried.

7
00:00:44.567 --> 00:00:49.236
"Ooh!" Dirk rolled on the floor.

8
00:00:49.237 --> 00:00:58.386
Brooklyn tried to get up, a little dazed. But she stumbled over Jacey's feet into Stuart.

9
00:00:58.387 --> 00:01:05.959
As Marv tried to help her up, Brooklyn's foot got caught in a bag of extra basketballs.

10
00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:12.886
Balls went spilling out and rolled onto the gym floor.

11
00:01:12.887 --> 00:01:16.949
"Oh no!" Brooklyn cried. "Sorry, Marv!"

12
00:01:16.951 --> 00:01:21.966
Marv rubbed his arm where Brooklyn had bumped into him.

13
00:01:21.967 --> 00:01:26.526
"It's okay, Brooklyn," he said as she scrambled to get the balls.

14
00:01:26.527 --> 00:01:30.544
His voice sounded tired. "They've got them."

15
00:01:30.545 --> 00:01:39.784
Marv was right. Jacey, Aaron, and a few other Whales were already scooping up the rolling balls.

16
00:01:39.785 --> 00:01:51.834
Brooklyn held the bag open. "Balls in here, guys." Then she heard loud moaning sounds and glanced up.

17
00:01:51.835 --> 00:02:00.764
Dirk held one of Coach Teagan's arms and was trying to help him up. But the coach was grimacing in pain.

18
00:02:00.765 --> 00:02:05.161
"Wait! Dirk, don't move him," Brooklyn said.

19
00:02:05.162 --> 00:02:15.658
"She's right. It could be serious." Marv pulled out his phone and called 911 for emergency medical help.

20
00:02:15.659 --> 00:02:23.231
Brooklyn hurried over to where Coach Teagan lay. He was wedged under the bleachers.

21
00:02:23.232 --> 00:02:29.484
"Ow!" Coach squeezed his eyes shut and gritted his teeth. "It hurts."

22
00:02:29.485 --> 00:02:38.057
Luckily for Coach Teagan, an ambulance arrived at the school in about eight minutes.

23
00:02:38.058 --> 00:02:45.120
No one on the Whales team seemed to be thinking about the game they'd lost anymore—they were all too worried about Coach.

24
00:02:45.121 --> 00:02:54.138
The players quickly shook hands with the Terriers, who then gathered up their gear and left to board their bus.

25
00:02:54.139 --> 00:03:01.376
Brooklyn and the rest of the team watched as two emergency medical workers attended to Coach Teagan.

26
00:03:01.377 --> 00:03:07.867
He struggled to get out from under the bleachers. "My wife needs me," he murmured.

27
00:03:07.868 --> 00:03:13.447
"Hold on, sir," a paramedic said. "We need to check your vital signs."

28
00:03:13.448 --> 00:03:22.698
While one medical worker put a cuff around Coach's arm to check his blood pressure, the other one set up a portable stretcher on wheels.

29
00:03:22.699 --> 00:03:27.698
"We're going to take you to Memorial Hospital for x-rays," she said.

30
00:03:27.699 --> 00:03:33.198
Coach groaned. "Someone had better call my wife!"

31
00:03:33.199 --> 00:03:40.587
"Coach and his wife are expecting babies any time now," Marv informed the medical workers. "Triplets."

32
00:03:40.588 --> 00:03:43.979
The paramedics raised their eyebrows in surprise.

33
00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:47.563
"Oh wow," the woman murmured.

34
00:03:47.564 --> 00:03:57.740
Brooklyn grabbed Jacey's arm and pointed to the other end of the bleachers. "I think Coach's phone flew that way. Let's find it!"

35
00:03:57.741 --> 00:04:04.327
The girls ran to look for the phone, and Brooklyn quickly spotted a black object lying on the floor.

36
00:04:04.328 --> 00:04:10.062
She picked it up. "This is just the phone's plastic cover. It's broken."

37
00:04:10.063 --> 00:04:20.304
"Here's the actual phone," Jacey said. She reached underneath the first row of bleachers. "Look. The screen is cracked."

38
00:04:20.305 --> 00:04:26.821
"That's not good." Brooklyn took the phone from Jacey. "I wonder if it still works."

39
00:04:26.822 --> 00:04:31.970
Suddenly it began ringing.

40
00:04:31.971 --> 00:04:39.800
"Hey!" Coach Teagan shouted from the stretcher. "That's my wife's ringtone! Brooklyn, answer it!"

41
00:04:39.801 --> 00:04:44.864
Brooklyn held the chipped phone carefully to her ear. "Hello?"

42
00:04:44.865 --> 00:04:48.318
Coach lifted his head. "She might be in labor!"

43
00:04:48.319 --> 00:04:53.028
"Hold still. Please, sir!" the emergency workers said.

44
00:04:53.029 --> 00:05:01.358
Brooklyn listened to the voice over the phone and then said, "I'll tell him." She ran over to Coach.

45
00:05:01.359 --> 00:05:07.183
"Your wife is in labor, Coach. A neighbor is driving her to the hospital right now."

46
00:05:07.184 --> 00:05:10.516
"Let's go!" Coach Teagan shouted.

47
00:05:10.517 --> 00:05:19.189
"We can meet your wife at the hospital, sir," the female paramedic said calmly. "There's no need to panic."

48
00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:25.086
"What's taking you two so long?" Coach snapped. "Let's move—now!"

49
00:05:25.087 --> 00:05:31.750
The Whales watched the medical workers roll Coach Teagan out of the gym.

50
00:05:31.751 --> 00:05:37.735
Brooklyn turned to Marv. "Will Coach be okay?" she asked.

51
00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:43.148
"It sounds like he hurt his hip. But I think he'll feel better once he sees his wife.

52
00:05:43.149 --> 00:05:49.409
The doctors and nurses will take good care of them both." Marv clapped his hands.

53
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:54.145
"Okay, team, speaking of labor, we have a lot of work to do.

54
00:05:54.146 --> 00:06:00.890
Play-offs start next week. If we stick together, we can win the league championship!"

55
00:06:00.891 --> 00:06:09.231
Brooklyn watched Marv rub his beard nervously. Coach's injury was really bad timing.

56
00:06:09.232 --> 00:06:13.719
Marv was going to have to prepare the team for play-offs on his own.

57
00:06:13.720 --> 00:06:21.801
"Hey, Marv," she said slowly. "With Coach out, you're going to need some help. I was thinking—"

58
00:06:21.802 --> 00:06:29.189
"No way!" Dirk cut her off. "You're not coaching me, Brooklyn. Or anybody else on this team!"

59
00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:33.952
Brooklyn's face flushed. She looked around at the rest of the team.

60
00:06:33.953 --> 00:06:38.873
A few kids were looking down. Jacey was shaking her head.

61
00:06:38.874 --> 00:06:43.018
She shrugged and mouthed, "Sorry" to Brooklyn.

62
00:06:43.019 --> 00:06:51.421
"I know I can help," Brooklyn insisted. "I know this team, and I know a lot about basketball."

63
00:06:51.422 --> 00:06:56.913
"Like you helped today?" Dirk scowled. "We lost the game."

64
00:06:56.914 --> 00:07:03.510
"Okay, Dirk. That's enough. We'll discuss everything at practice on Monday," Marv said.

65
00:07:03.511 --> 00:07:13.922
"Now let's close up the gym." He went into the gym office and began clicking off the overhead lights.

66
00:07:13.923 --> 00:07:22.566
Dirk stood frowning in the shadows under the basketball net. "We're not much of a team without a head coach," he muttered.

67
00:07:22.567 --> 00:07:26.995
"You're right, Dirk," Jacey said. "This is bad."

68
00:07:26.996 --> 00:07:34.135
Aaron shrugged and pulled on his warm-up jacket. "We've got Marv," he said.

69
00:07:34.136 --> 00:07:38.818
His arms were so long that the jacket's sleeves barely reached his wrists.

70
00:07:38.819 --> 00:07:46.649
"My dad said everyone called him 'Marvelous Marv' when he played hoops in college, so Marv must know what he's doing."

71
00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:54.371
"You've got me too!" Brooklyn chimed in. "I've got a notebook filled with cool plays we can practice for the play-offs."

72
00:07:54.372 --> 00:08:00.288
Dirk snorted. "We won't make it very far in the play-offs. We're losers."

73
00:08:00.289 --> 00:08:10.044
"No, we're still a great team!" Brooklyn said. She grabbed a ball and dribbled it closer to Dirk.

74
00:08:10.045 --> 00:08:16.614
Maybe Dirk didn't like the idea of her coaching, but he loved basketball and the team.

75
00:08:16.615 --> 00:08:24.859
"I can win him over," Brooklyn thought. She suddenly held up the basketball. "Catch, Dirk!"

76
00:08:24.860 --> 00:08:33.274
Dirk's hands went up automatically. But just as Brooklyn tossed the ball, the gym went completely dark.

77
00:08:33.275 --> 00:08:38.937
"Ow!" shouted Dirk a second later. "My nose!"

78
00:08:38.938 --> 00:08:48.138
Brooklyn cringed. "Sorry, Dirk!"
